Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?comms:=20RSS=20Feeds=20account=20visible=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20root-cause=20synchronize=20flag=20+=20engine=20guar?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ds?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adding an RSS account showed NO folders: the synthetic Feeds account was created
with synchronize=false (CommsAccounts.ensureRssAccount) while every folder/drawer
query filters account.synchronize (DaoFolder.liveFolders + ~10 siblings, DaoAccount
drawer) → zero rows → empty UI.

Flip synchronize=true (chosen over amending ~10 query surfaces). The sync engines
still never touch it: ServiceSynchronize gates each account on SUM(folder.synchronize)>0
and feed folders keep synchronize=false. Plus the two real leaks that flag would open:
- EntityOperation: new inlineRSS() drops/locally-applies message ops for TYPE_RSS
  (mirrors inlinePOP3); sync() short-circuits feed folders to WorkerFeedSync.oneShot
  so pull-to-refresh = immediate feed poll, not a SYNC op against the hostless account.
- ServiceSynchronize.monitorAccount: TYPE_RSS guard (defense in depth, mirrors JMAP).
- CommsAccounts.repairRssAccount(): startup one-shot flips synchronize on for pre-0053
  installs + drops stale ops (wired in ApplicationEx next to repairJmapFolders).
- WorkerFeedSync.oneShot(): immediate one-shot poll.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
